    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d418">

                <pb facs="0591" n="495" xml:id="pg495"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Señor Romero.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-12-04"><hi rendition="#italic">December 4,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 66.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the habeas corpus cases in the
                    western district of Texas, which you desired might be appealed and brought
                    before the Supreme Court of the United States at an early date, I regret to say
                    that the Attorney-General notified me by note, copy of which I inclose, that the
                    time within which an appeal can be taken has expired, and that consequently an
                    appeal can not be directed.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d418-a1.xml" xpointer="d418-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
